## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design bounded-local dynamic structures with clear trade-offs for batched updates and exact counts.

## Key Concepts
- Local inversions with distance d
- Batched point updates
- Maintaining cross-pair indicators with O(d) per update

## Code Example
```javascript
// initialize b_t and S
for (let t=1; t<=d; t++) for (let i=1; i<=n-t; i++) b[t][i] = a[i] > a[i+t];
let S = sumAll(b);
// on update (i, v)
a[i] = v;
for (let t=1; t<=d; t++) {
  if (i <= n-t) S += (b[t][i] ? -1 : 0), b[t][i] = a[i] > a[i+t]; S += (b[t][i] ? 1 : 0);
  if (i-t >= 1) S += (b[t][i-t] ? -1 : 0), b[t][i-t] = a[i-t] > a[i]; S += (b[t][i-t] ? 1 : 0);
}
console.log(S);
```

